{
  "requirement": "The SDK offers this `Sources` method. Its source tools expose the\n`search_text` command.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Sources {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Search available project files.\n    pub async fn search_text(&self, query: &TextQuery) -> Result<TextMatches, SourceError>;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations.** The requirement has two structural obligations:\n1. `Sources` offers `pub async fn search_text(&self, query: &TextQuery) -> Result<TextMatches, SourceError>`.\n2. The source tools expose the `search_text` command.\n\n**Method signature.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/public.rs#impl[Sources]/fn[search_text]` is declared in the non-generic `impl Sources`. It has exactly the required signature: `pub async fn`, `&self`, `query: &TextQuery`, returning `Result<TextMatches, SourceError>`.\n- It delegates to `self.analysis.provider.search_text(query)`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs#trait[SourceProvider]/fn[search_text]` takes `&TextQuery` and has a default body that calls `defaults::search_text`. This is the interface the method delegates through.\n- `TextQuery` is a struct in `public.rs`. Its fields include `scope` and `pattern`. `SourceSession::dispatch` also sets `context_lines` and `limit`.\n\n**Tool exposure.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/sources.rs#impl[SourceSession<…>/ToolSession<D>]/fn[definitions]` registers a `search_text` tool. Its parameters are `pattern` (required), `prefix`, `context_lines` and `limit`.\n- The `search_text` arm of `fn[dispatch]` in the same impl builds a `TextQuery` and calls `provider.search_text`. It returns the matches as JSON.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#impl[Session<'_, D>/ToolSession<D>]/fn[dispatch]` also dispatches `search_text`, through `self.tools.sources.search_text(&TextQuery {...})`. This is the `Sources` method itself.\n\n**Gaps.** I found no structural gap and no conflicting element. No `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply. Tests also exercise `search_text` through the tool dispatch and the `Sources` method, for example the tests in `agent/tests.rs` and `sources/tests.rs`. Test adequacy is not at issue for this signature-only requirement.",
  "references": "adb051f12dd0a86e8a4f3fb46412c455aa1de1be9588c7f7d09c8aa3237dc669",
